  "slug": "2024-nhl-entry-draft",
  "summary": "The 2024 NHL Entry Draft was held June 28–29 at Sphere in Paradise, Nevada. The San Jose Sharks made Macklin Celebrini the first overall pick, followed by Chicago’s Artyom Levshunov and Anaheim’s Beckett Sennecke. Draft rights held by the deactivated Arizona Coyotes transferred to the Utah Hockey Club.\n\nSan Jose and Chicago won the two draft lotteries on May 7. The results did not change the draft order, the first time that had happened since 2010. Chicago, which picked first in 2023 and second in 2024, remained eligible for the 2025 lottery.\n\nEligible players were born between January 1, 2004, and September 15, 2006, with additional eligibility for certain undrafted non-North American players born in 2003 and unsigned 2022 draftees born after June 30, 2004. Numerous picks changed hands through trades, including several first- and second-round selections.",
